  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Friday) \nIssued at 846 PM CST Fri Nov 27 2026\n\nThe start of the long term period will see zonal flow aloft and\nbuilding high pressure to our SW. The building high pressure will\nallow a gradual warming trend through mid week with highs warming\nfrom the low 50s to the mid 60s by Wednesday. Through the second half\nof the work week, the surface high pressure will pass to our east and\ninduce a solid return flow pattern. This will result in much warmer\ntemperatures for Thursday and Friday. Highs will warm into the \nhigh 60s to potentially low 70s, about 10+ degrees above normal \nfor early December. Dew points will increase in conjunction with \ntemperatures, rising to at least the 50s. The seasonal warm and \nmoist conditions look to be short lived as our next low pressure \nsystem looks to move through on Friday. Long range models \ncurrently disagree on depth and forward speed of the parent mid \nlevel low, leading to a decent amount of uncertainty regarding \nintensity and timing. We will have to keep an eye on this system \nas it gets closer especially with the unseasonably warm and moist \nsurface conditions in place by the end of the week.",
